    definition: 'Rather than trying to synchronize 32 wires simultaneously, TX holds the 32-bit `data` bus completely static while sending a single 1-bit `req` across a 2-FF synchronizer. RX reads the already-stable 32-bit `data` cleanly and returns `ack` through a 2-FF synchronizer back to TX.',
