    year: 'Foundational Mechanism',
    tagline: 'Enables full 1-word-per-cycle back-to-back streaming across unrelated clocks using single-bit-changing Gray pointers.',
    definition: 'An Asynchronous FIFO stores data in a dual-port SRAM/regfile with `wptr` in `wclk` and `rptr` in `rclk`. Converting binary pointers to Gray code (`bin ^ (bin >> 1)`) guarantees ONLY ONE BIT ever toggles per increment, so a 2-FF synchronizer can NEVER sample an invalid multi-bit intermediate value.',
